        "raw": "<p>Totally stealing &quot;default defaults&quot; as a phrase, just so you know.</p><p>Yeah, at first, I thought they should be nemeses, but then I realized that neither Paul nor Pauline would be that keen to attack him, and he would, if anything, break off from a fight to keep Pauline from dying again. &nbsp;Arguably, he might act nemesis-ey towards an earlier version of himself, but the reverse-nemesis thing works better in my book. &nbsp;It does make Lead From The Front even crazier than it already is, but even with the damage penalty, Legacy will probably go down in 1-2 turns under all that abuse, so hey.</p><p>The thing I do find odd is that Visionary isn&#39;t his nemesis, though. &nbsp;Didn&#39;t she come back in time to prevent him from existing? &nbsp;I know they ran out of space for more icons and all, but it&#39;s sadistic to give nemesis status to someone like Unity, who should never go in against IL, ever, and not Visionary, the only hero who has faced him before on her non-promo version.</p><p>Ironic</p>",
